  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNODC Strengthening capacities against deforestation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen national capacities for the surveillance and control of deforestation. Define and improve procedures for preventive surveillance, judiciary and disciplinary intervention, Support the implementation of administrative and judiciary actions for the control of deforestation in focal areas. The project aims to contribute to strengthen capacities of Colombian authorities through establishing two education programs at post-graduate level and one online-learning platform. Partner institutions are: Attorney General&#x2019;s Office (FGN), the Ministry of Environment and Sustainable Development, the Ministry of Defense, the National Police (DJIN/DICAR), Office of the Inspector General of the Nation (PGN), Office of the Presidential Counsellor for Management and Compliance, National Natural Parks, Regional Autonomous Corporations CDA and CORPOAMAZONIA, Superintendence of Notary and Registry, and the Financial Information Analysis Unit. The project includes the development of protocols for institutional actions, support to inter-institutional coordination, diagnostic, research and operations in four (4) deforestation hot-spots.</narrative>
  </description>
